\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {A/B dissociation (measured).} (a)~Data-side $\tau $ of E$^2$-JEPA latents: one narrow band. (b)~Model-side $\tau $ of the same latents: three orders of magnitude. (c)~LeWM's model-side spectrum: exactly $7$ neutral modes, equal to the dimension of the physical state---the protocol recovers a known ground truth, and the dynamics provably contain the multi-scale structure that the coordinates lack.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ab}{{2}{4}{\textbf {A/B dissociation (measured).} (a)~Data-side $\tau $ of E$^2$-JEPA latents: one narrow band. (b)~Model-side $\tau $ of the same latents: three orders of magnitude. (c)~LeWM's model-side spectrum: exactly $7$ neutral modes, equal to the dimension of the physical state---the protocol recovers a known ground truth, and the dynamics provably contain the multi-scale structure that the coordinates lack}{figure.2}{}}
